  "skills": [
    {
      "id": "m7-operations",
      "name": "The four operations and their order (BODMAS) in ℕ"
    },
    {
      "id": "m7-powers",
      "name": "Whole number powers"
    }
  ],
  "note": {
    "status": "draft",
    "text": "A power is a short way to write a repeated multiplication:\n2⁵ = 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 × 2 = 32.\nWe read 2⁵ as '2 to the power 5'. The 2 is the base and the 5 is the exponent (index).\n• a² is 'a squared': 7² = 49.\n• a³ is 'a cubed': 4³ = 64.\nBe careful: 2⁵ is not 2 × 5.\n\nWhen a calculation has several operations, follow BODMAS: Brackets first, then Orders (powers), then Division and Multiplication from left to right, then Addition and Subtraction from left to right.\n3 + 2 × 4² = 3 + 2 × 16 = 3 + 32 = 35.\n\nIn ℕ, adding or multiplying two natural numbers always gives a natural number. The order does not matter: 5 + 8 = 8 + 5 and 5 × 8 = 8 × 5. Also 3 × (4 + 5) = 3 × 4 + 3 × 5. But a − b is in ℕ only when a ≥ b.",
    "checks": [
      "2 ^ 5 == 32",
      "2 * 2 * 2 * 2 * 2 == 32",
      "7 ^ 2 == 49",
      "4 ^ 3 == 64",
      "2 ^ 5 != 2 * 5",
      "3 + 2 * 4 ^ 2 == 35",
      "2 * 16 == 32",
      "5 + 8 == 8 + 5",
      "5 * 8 == 8 * 5",
      "3 * (4 + 5) == 3 * 4 + 3 * 5"
    ]
  },
  "worked_example": {
    "status": "draft",
    "vars": {
      "a": 7,
      "b": 3,
      "c": 9,
      "d": 5,
      "two": 2
    },
    "problem": "Calculate {a} + {b} × ({c} − {d}){sup(two)}.",
    "steps": [
      "Brackets first: {c} − {d} = {c - d}.",
      "Orders (powers) next: {c - d}{sup(two)} = {c - d} × {c - d} = {(c - d) ^ two}.",
      "Then multiplication: {b} × {(c - d) ^ two} = {b * (c - d) ^ two}.",
      "Finally addition: {a} + {b * (c - d) ^ two} = {a + b * (c - d) ^ two}."
    ],
    "answer": "{a} + {b} × ({c} − {d}){sup(two)} = {a + b * (c - d) ^ two}",
    "checks": [
      "a + b * (c - d) ^ two == a + b * ((c - d) * (c - d))",
      "(a + b) * (c - d) ^ two != a + b * (c - d) ^ two"
    ]
  },
